  "response_text": "The HAL is a hardware abstraction layer. It is useful in connecting the software of the computer, in this case the IDE, with the hardware of the Nucleo microcontroller. It is used within a general embedded project to control machines through transmitting information. For instance, in this lab, numbers were transmitted through a function involving HAL between the hardware and the software. The HAL is not necessarily a necessity, but rather a convenience to operate low-level functions within the hardware.\\n",
